;; Simplify checked against the Rocq semantics of Flambda 2: each example
;; X.fl is run before and after Simplify on the machine extracted from
;; middle_end/flambda2/rocq/FlambdaSemanticsSpec.v, and what the two runs
;; come to is compared (see ../tools/flsemantics.ml). The tool fails if
;; they differ; what it prints is kept in X.expected, beside X.fl.
;;
;; To add an example, add X.fl (its module symbol must match its name) and
;; X.expected, and nothing else: there is no list of examples to add it
;; to. `dune promote` writes X.expected, or updates it, from what the tool
;; printed. Each example is run on its own, as the compiler keeps its
;; symbols from one unit to the next.
;;
;; The rules are made from the .fl files that are here: gen_rules.sh writes
;; one rule to run each example and one to compare what it prints with
;; its expected file. They are included by run/dune and not by this file,
;; which dune has to read before it can say which .fl files are here. The
;; runtest alias of this directory takes in that of run/.

(rule
 (deps
  (glob_files *.fl)
  (glob_files *.expected))
 (action
  (with-stdout-to
   dune.inc
   (run sh %{dep:gen_rules.sh} %{deps}))))
